// Doom's fixed point, angle tables and random numbers in ent-lang
// (examples/doom: fixed.ent, tables.ent, angles.ent, random.ent), by what
// they give for a million pairs of numbers. The numbers here are those of
// the C they were ported from: examples/doom/check/maths.sh compares the
// two, where the reference is there (examples/doom/reference/fetch.sh).
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/doom %S/../../examples/doom/check/maths.ent | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:      tables 1855389718 3561017569 479422538
// CHECK-NEXT: 0: 1015568748 1586005467 mul 1491847289 div 41964 slope 618 angle 873410239
// CHECK-NEXT:   dist 2147483647 aprox 2093789841
// CHECK:      900000: -827960916 -27782 mul 350988924 div 2147483647 slope 117 angle 2147483648
// CHECK-NEXT:   dist 827973549 aprox 827974807
// CHECK-NEXT: mul 3416598475 div 1762905654 slope 1833318430
// CHECK-NEXT: angle 2373923027 dist 1311878617 aprox 1150365838
// CHECK-NEXT: random 3100241346 at 88
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
